# Backlog / Future Work

## 0.4.0: FastFileIndex

The index becomes its own package, `FastFileIndex`, backed by MFTLib as the NTFS driver and by new macOS
(`getattrlistbulk` plus FSEvents) and Linux (`getdents64` plus `statx`, fanotify or inotify) drivers behind one
public backend contract. The plan, measurements, ordering and every child issue live on the
[0.4 epic, issue 913](https://gitea.fleet.sticktoitive.net/schoen/MFTLib/issues/913); query the
`ship:mftlib-0.4.0` label across MFTLib, file-wizard and git-wizard for the board.

## Packed Index Follow-Ups (deferred)

- **Children table (CSR)**: revisit when measured tree UI expand latency exceeds 50 ms.
- **Name interning**: revisit when the measured name pool exceeds 40 percent of block size.
- **Secondary name index**: revisit when the median warm exact or substring `FileIndex.Search` query exceeds 200 ms (`Benchmark.exe index --cache-directory <path> --iterations 3`).
- **Hard links as multiple rows per record**: revisit when a consumer needs the second name.

